\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Ranks on the square and four-dimensional torus}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The based-cell basis in \ref{fdip-00VR} gives
##{\begin{array}{c|c|c}
 n&\text{right }\mathcal O_k\text{-rank}&k\text{-rank}\\ \hline
 2&4|X|&16|X|\\
 4&16|X|&64|X|
 \end{array}}
For the one-site square torus, #{|X|=1}. Its vertex,
two labeled edges and face carry #{4} independent
Hurwitz coefficients, hence #{16} scalar coefficients.
These are free-module ranks over the declared algebras.}
